What this license covers, and what the built core contains

The license above covers this repository's own code: the glue in go/chimera,
the stand-in packages in go/sdl2 and go/reisen, the patches, the scripts in
waterbox/ and tools/, and the documents.

The core package built from it (ikemen.chimeraCore) also contains, each under
its own terms (the package's licenses/ folder holds every text):

- Ikemen GO 1.0.0 (MIT), compiled from the submodule extern/Ikemen-GO with
  patches/ applied, and its engine files (data/, external/, font/) carried
  inside the core;
- the Go 1.27.3 runtime and standard library (BSD-3-Clause), with
  waterbox/go-patches applied;
- the Go modules Ikemen GO is built from (MIT, BSD, Apache-2.0, the FreeType
  License and the Unlicense; build/licenses/go-modules.txt when packaged);
- libxmp 4.7.4 (MIT), which plays module music;
- Mesa 24.0.9 (MIT), whose llvmpipe driver behind OSMesa is the OpenGL the
  game draws with, with waterbox/mesa-patches applied;
- LLVM 18.1.8 (Apache-2.0 with the LLVM exception), which llvmpipe compiles
  shaders with;
- musl and the miniBox guest kit (MIT).

The package carries no game and no screenpack: the project brings the game
folder as a zip. The test game the scripts make (tests/make-test-game.sh) is
the Ikemen GO screenpack from the submodule extern/Ikemen-GO-Screenpack; most
of it is CC BY 3.0, and Elecbyte's part of it (Kung Fu Man, two stages and the
MUGEN fonts) is under Elecbyte's own non-commercial terms. It is never part of
the package.
